IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dda-core`
IMPORT `dda-seat`

-- Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) -- cases for the claimant's seat (dda-seat.l4), every exported question, with a few on
-- the dda-core.l4 functions the seat composes (the Schedule 1 relevant dates). Every expected value was worked by hand
-- from the deposited text of the Act and the Dust Diseases Regulations 2021 (the provision is named on each group),
-- never copied from the encoding's output. Edges: the day before and the day of 8 February 2006; the day before and the
-- day of each Schedule 1 relevant date (1 January 1940, 1 January 1960, 1 July 1971, 1 January 1976); 20 and 21
-- employees (a prescribed business employs more than 20); the insurer's cap at, just under and just over the indemnity.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the claimant`

-- Short names for the answers.
`dda yes` MEANS `yes: it is a dust disease action, and the Act's procedures apply to it (s 3)`
`dda not disease` MEANS `no: the disease is not a dust disease, which in this Act means asbestosis, asbestos induced carcinoma, asbestos related pleural disease, mesothelioma, or another disease or condition resulting from exposure to asbestos dust (s 3)`
`dda not action` MEANS `no: it is not a dust disease action, which must be a civil action claiming damages for the dust disease (or a death from it) and asserting that another person's breach of duty caused it wholly or partly (s 3)`

`applies` MEANS `yes: the Act applies to causes of action arising and actions commenced before or after its commencement on 8 February 2006 (Sch 1 cl 4(1))`
`old trial` MEANS `no: the action was commenced, and its trial had commenced, before 8 February 2006, so the Act does not apply to it (Sch 1 cl 4(2))`

`saet` MEANS `SAET has jurisdiction to hear and determine it, and the jurisdiction is assigned to the South Australian Employment Court (s 4A(1), (2)); the Act also speaks of dust disease actions in the District Court (ss 5, 7 to 10)`
`saet none` MEANS `not covered: s 4A gives SAET jurisdiction over dust disease actions only`

`join same` MEANS `yes: the other claim arises from the same cause of action, so it may be included in the proceedings even though it does not relate to a dust disease (s 4A(4))`
`join ancillary` MEANS `yes: the matter is ancillary or related to the subject of the proceedings, so it may be included (s 4A(5))`
`join neither` MEANS `not covered: s 4A(4) and (5) allow only a claim from the same cause of action, or an ancillary or related matter, to be included`
`join not saet` MEANS `not covered: s 4A(4) and (5) speak only of proceedings in SAET on a dust disease action or a contribution claim`

`priority` MEANS `yes: the District Court or SAET will give directions so that the action has priority over less urgent cases and is dealt with as expeditiously as the proper administration of justice allows (s 5)`
`priority none` MEANS `not covered: s 5 gives priority to dust disease actions only`

`costs dc` MEANS `on the same basis as for other actions in the District Court (s 7(1))`
`costs saet` MEANS `on the same basis as for actions in the District Court (s 7(1a))`
`costs mc` MEANS `on the same basis as for a civil action in the Magistrates Court, because the action is within the Magistrates Court's jurisdictional limits and the court considers that appropriate (s 7(2))`
`costs none` MEANS `not covered: s 7 deals only with dust disease actions in the District Court or SAET`

`cause yes` MEANS `yes: it will be presumed that the exposure to asbestos dust caused or contributed to the dust disease, unless the contrary is proved (s 8(1))`
`cause rebutted` MEANS `no: the contrary has been proved, so the s 8(1) presumption gives way and causation is decided on the evidence (s 8(1))`
`cause unestablished` MEANS `no: s 8(1) gives no presumption on these facts: it must first be established that the person suffers or suffered from a dust disease and was exposed to asbestos dust in circumstances in which the exposure might have caused or contributed to it`
`cause none` MEANS `not covered: s 8(1) applies in a dust disease action`

`knew yes` MEANS `yes: the person who carried on the process is presumed to have known at the time that exposure to asbestos dust could result in a dust disease, unless the contrary is proved (s 8(2))`
`knew rebutted` MEANS `no: the contrary has been proved, so the s 8(2) presumption gives way (s 8(2))`
`knew not prescribed` MEANS `no: the process is not a prescribed industrial or commercial process at that time (s 8(2), reg 4 and Sch 1)`
`knew no exposure` MEANS `no: s 8(2) applies only to a process that could have resulted in the exposure of another person to asbestos dust`

`ev yes` MEANS `yes, the court may: it may admit evidence admitted in an earlier dust disease action against the same defendant, including one in a court or tribunal of the Commonwealth or another State or Territory (s 8(3)(a))`
`ev other` MEANS `not covered: s 8(3)(a) speaks only of evidence admitted in an earlier dust disease action against the same defendant`
`ev none` MEANS `not covered: s 8(3)(a) applies only in a dust disease action before the District Court or SAET`

`proof dispensed` MEANS `the court may dispense with proof of it, because it appears to the court to be not seriously in dispute (s 8(3)(b))`
`proof needed` MEANS `not covered: s 8(3)(b) lets the court dispense only with proof of a matter that appears to it to be not seriously in dispute`
`proof none` MEANS `not covered: s 8(3)(b) applies only in a dust disease action before the District Court or SAET`

`adm yes` MEANS `yes, the court may: a party who declines the court's invitation to admit facts of a formal nature, or facts peripheral to the major issues, may be ordered to pay the costs of proving them (s 8(3)(c))`
`adm no` MEANS `no: s 8(3)(c) lets the court award those costs only against a party who declined its invitation to admit the facts`
`adm major` MEANS `not covered: s 8(3)(c) speaks only of facts of a formal nature or facts peripheral to the major issues in dispute`
`adm none` MEANS `not covered: s 8(3)(c) applies only in a dust disease action before the District Court or SAET`

`find yes` MEANS `yes: the court may admit the earlier finding in evidence and indicate that it proposes to make a corresponding finding, which it will make unless the party who would be adversely affected satisfies it that the finding is inappropriate to the present case (s 8(4))`
`find resisted` MEANS `no: the party adversely affected has satisfied the court that a corresponding finding is inappropriate to the present case (s 8(4))`
`find body` MEANS `no: s 8(4) applies only to a finding made in a dust disease action by a court of South Australia, or a court or tribunal of the Commonwealth or another State or Territory`
`find irrelevant` MEANS `no: s 8(4) applies only to a finding the court considers relevant to the action before it`
`find none` MEANS `not covered: s 8(4) applies to an action under this Act before the District Court or SAET`

`later yes` MEANS `yes, the court may: award damages now on the assumption that you will not develop another dust disease, and award further damages at a future date if you do (s 9(1))`
`later no` MEANS `no: s 9(1) gives no deferred award on these facts: it must be proved or admitted that you may develop another dust disease wholly or partly as a result of the same breach of duty`
`later none` MEANS `not covered: s 9(1) applies in a dust disease action`

`ex yes` MEANS `yes: the court should award exemplary damages against this defendant (s 9(2))`
`ex no a` MEANS `no: s 9(2) does not direct an award of exemplary damages on these facts, because it is not shown that the defendant knew of the risk of exposure or carried on a Schedule 2 process that resulted in the exposure (s 9(2)(a)); the general law of exemplary damages is untouched`
`ex no b` MEANS `no: s 9(2) does not direct an award of exemplary damages on these facts, because it is not shown that the defendant knew at the time that exposure to asbestos dust could result in a dust disease (s 9(2)(b)); the general law of exemplary damages is untouched`
`ex none` MEANS `not covered: s 9(2) applies in a dust disease action`

`dom yes` MEANS `yes: the court must compensate the loss or impairment of your capacity to perform domestic services for another person as a separate head of damage, despite any other Act or law (s 9(3))`
`dom no loss` MEANS `not covered: s 9(3) speaks only of a loss or impairment of the capacity to perform domestic services for another person`
`dom none` MEANS `not covered: s 9(3) applies in a dust disease action`

`order first` MEANS `yes: liability and the amount of liability to the plaintiff are decided first, before contribution between the defendants or insurers (s 10)`
`order together` MEANS `not necessarily: the court considers that any delay from dealing with the questions together is inconsequential, so it may decide them together (s 10)`
`order none` MEANS `not covered: s 10 applies where several defendants or insurers are involved in a dust disease action`

`ins yes` MEANS `yes: the action may be brought directly against the insurer who insured the defendant against the liability, and the insurer has the same rights, powers, duties and liabilities as the defendant would have had (s 11(1), (2))`
`ins no status` MEANS `no: s 11(1) gives no direct action on these facts: the defendant must be dead or dissolved, insolvent, or unable to be found`
`ins no cover` MEANS `no: s 11(1) gives a direct action only against an insurer who insured the defendant against a liability to which the action relates`
`ins none` MEANS `not covered: s 11 applies to a dust disease action`

`appeal single` MEANS `to the Supreme Court constituted of a single Judge (s 11A(a))`
`appeal ca` MEANS `to the Court of Appeal (s 11A(b))`
`appeal none` MEANS `not covered: s 11A deals only with appeals from SAET in or about a dust disease action`

`meso` MEANS `mesothelioma`
`other disease` MEANS `another disease or pathological condition`
`p mining` MEANS `mining or milling of asbestos, or associated packing or transportation of asbestos`
`p manufacture` MEANS `manufacture of asbestos products`
`p maker use` MEANS `use of asbestos products by their manufacturer`
`p design` MEANS `design of an object or thing containing asbestos or asbestos products`
`p supply` MEANS `sale or other supply of asbestos products by someone other than their manufacturer`
`p install` MEANS `installation of asbestos products`
`p use` MEANS `use of asbestos products by someone other than their manufacturer`
`p item 10` MEANS `another industrial or commercial process involving asbestos or asbestos products`
`p none` MEANS `a process not involving asbestos`

§§ `s 3: dust disease and dust disease action`

-- (a) to (d) are dust diseases whatever the cause answer; (e) needs asbestos dust.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dda yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dda yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dda yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `asbestos induced carcinoma` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dda yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `asbestos related pleural disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dda yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `other disease` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dda yes`
-- Silicosis (another disease, not from asbestos dust): not a dust disease in this Act.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dda not disease`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `other disease` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `dda not disease`
-- Each limb of the "dust disease action" definition failing in turn.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `meso` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `dda not action`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `meso` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dda not action`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a dust disease action` `asbestosis` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `dda not action`

§§ `Sch 1 cl 4: actions the Act applies to (commencement 8 February 2006)`

#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my action` (`the date` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `applies`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my action` (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 9 2027) EQUALS `applies`
-- Commenced and tried before commencement.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my action` (`the date` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2005) EQUALS `old trial`
-- The last day before commencement for both.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my action` (`the date` 7 2 2006) TRUE (`the date` 7 2 2006) EQUALS `old trial`
-- Trial began on the day of commencement: not "before".
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my action` (`the date` 7 2 2006) TRUE (`the date` 8 2 2006) EQUALS `applies`
-- Commenced before, trial not yet begun (the date given is ignored).
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my action` (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2005) EQUALS `applies`
-- Commenced on the day of commencement.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my action` (`the date` 8 2 2006) TRUE (`the date` 8 2 2006) EQUALS `applies`

§§ `s 4A: forum and joinder`

#ASSERT `Where can I bring my dust disease action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `saet`
#ASSERT `Where can I bring my dust disease action` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `saet none`
#ASSERT `Where can I bring my dust disease action` `asbestosis` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `saet none`

#ASSERT `Can I include another claim in my SAET proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `join same`
#ASSERT `Can I include another claim in my SAET proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `join same`
#ASSERT `Can I include another claim in my SAET proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `join ancillary`
#ASSERT `Can I include another claim in my SAET proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `join neither`
#ASSERT `Can I include another claim in my SAET proceedings` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `join not saet`

§§ `s 5: priority`

#ASSERT `Will my action be given priority` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `priority`
#ASSERT `Will my action be given priority` `other disease` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `priority`
#ASSERT `Will my action be given priority` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `priority none`

§§ `s 7: costs`

#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the District Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs dc`
#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs saet`
-- Within the Magistrates Court's limits, but the court does not consider its basis appropriate.
#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the District Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `costs dc`
#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `costs saet`
#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the District Court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `costs mc`
#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `costs mc`
-- The court's view without the action being within the limits.
#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `costs saet`
#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `another court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `costs none`
#ASSERT `On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE `the District Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs none`

§§ `s 8(1): presumed causation`

#ASSERT `Will it be presumed that my exposure caused my disease` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cause yes`
#ASSERT `Will it be presumed that my exposure caused my disease` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `cause rebutted`
#ASSERT `Will it be presumed that my exposure caused my disease` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cause unestablished`
#ASSERT `Will it be presumed that my exposure caused my disease` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cause unestablished`
#ASSERT `Will it be presumed that my exposure caused my disease` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cause none`

§§ `s 8(2), reg 4, Sch 1: presumed knowledge`

-- Items 1 to 5 from 1 January 1940.
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p mining` 5 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1940) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew yes`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p mining` 5 FALSE (`the date` 31 12 1939) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew not prescribed`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p manufacture` 500 FALSE (`the date` 1 6 1955) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew yes`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p maker use` 500 FALSE (`the date` 1 6 1955) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `knew rebutted`
-- Items 6 to 9: a prescribed business (more than 20 persons) from 1 January 1960, any other from 1 July 1971.
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p install` 21 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew yes`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p install` 21 FALSE (`the date` 31 12 1959) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew not prescribed`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p install` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew not prescribed`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p install` 20 FALSE (`the date` 30 6 1971) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew not prescribed`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p install` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 7 1971) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew yes`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p design` 100 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1965) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew yes`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p supply` 3 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1965) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew not prescribed`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p use` 3 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1980) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew yes`
-- Item 10 from 1 January 1976, but not where the only asbestos is in the premises' structure.
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p item 10` 3 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1976) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew yes`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p item 10` 3 FALSE (`the date` 31 12 1975) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew not prescribed`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p item 10` 300 TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew not prescribed`
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p none` 300 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `knew not prescribed`
-- A prescribed process that could not have exposed anyone.
#ASSERT `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `p mining` 5 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1950) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `knew no exposure`

-- The Schedule 1 relevant dates directly.
#ASSERT `the relevant date (Sch 1 cl 2)` `p mining` 0 EQUALS `the date` 1 1 1940
#ASSERT `the relevant date (Sch 1 cl 2)` `p supply` 21 EQUALS `the date` 1 1 1960
#ASSERT `the relevant date (Sch 1 cl 2)` `p supply` 20 EQUALS `the date` 1 7 1971
#ASSERT `the relevant date (Sch 1 cl 2)` `p item 10` 1000 EQUALS `the date` 1 1 1976
#ASSERT `is prescribed for s 9(2) (reg 5)` `p maker use` (`the date` 1 1 1940)
#ASSERT (NOT (`is prescribed for s 9(2) (reg 5)` `p install` (`the date` 1 1 1990)))

§§ `s 8(3) and (4): evidence and earlier findings`

#ASSERT `Can earlier evidence against the same defendant be used in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the District Court` TRUE EQUALS `ev yes`
#ASSERT `Can earlier evidence against the same defendant be used in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE EQUALS `ev yes`
#ASSERT `Can earlier evidence against the same defendant be used in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` FALSE EQUALS `ev other`
#ASSERT `Can earlier evidence against the same defendant be used in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `another court` TRUE EQUALS `ev none`
#ASSERT `Can earlier evidence against the same defendant be used in my action` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE EQUALS `ev none`

#ASSERT `Must I prove a matter not seriously in dispute` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE EQUALS `proof dispensed`
#ASSERT `Must I prove a matter not seriously in dispute` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the District Court` FALSE EQUALS `proof needed`
#ASSERT `Must I prove a matter not seriously in dispute` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `another court` TRUE EQUALS `proof none`

#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay the costs of proving facts I would not admit` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `adm yes`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay the costs of proving facts I would not admit` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `adm no`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay the costs of proving facts I would not admit` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `adm no`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay the costs of proving facts I would not admit` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the District Court` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `adm major`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay the costs of proving facts I would not admit` `meso` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the District Court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `adm none`

#ASSERT `Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE `a court of South Australia` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `find yes`
#ASSERT `Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the District Court` TRUE `a court or tribunal of the Commonwealth or another State or Territory` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `find yes`
#ASSERT `Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE `a court of South Australia` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `find resisted`
#ASSERT `Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE `a court of South Australia` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `find irrelevant`
#ASSERT `Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE `a South Australian tribunal that is not a court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `find body`
#ASSERT `Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` TRUE `a court or tribunal outside Australia` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `find body`
#ASSERT `Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `SAET` FALSE `a court of South Australia` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `find body`
#ASSERT `Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `another court` TRUE `a court of South Australia` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `find none`

§§ `s 9(1): damages now and later`

#ASSERT `Can I get damages now and more later if I develop another dust disease` `asbestosis` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `later yes`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages now and more later if I develop another dust disease` `asbestosis` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `later no`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages now and more later if I develop another dust disease` `asbestosis` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `later none`

§§ `s 9(2): exemplary damages (with s 8(2) and regs 4, 5)`

-- Limb (a) by knowledge of the risk, limb (b) on the evidence.
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `p none` 5 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1985) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ex yes`
-- Limb (a) by a Schedule 2 process from 1 January 1940; limb (b) by the s 8(2) presumption.
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `p mining` 5 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1940) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ex yes`
-- The day before 1 January 1940: neither limb from the process.
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `p mining` 5 FALSE (`the date` 31 12 1939) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ex no a`
-- The presumption rebutted, and no other evidence of knowledge.
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `p manufacture` 50 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ex no b`
-- Rebutted presumption, but the court is satisfied on the evidence anyway.
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `p manufacture` 50 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ex yes`
-- Installation is in Schedule 1 but not Schedule 2: limb (a) needs knowledge of the risk.
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `p install` 21 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ex no a`
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `p install` 21 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ex yes`
-- 20 persons on 1 January 1960: no presumption until 1 July 1971, so limb (b) fails.
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `p install` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ex no b`
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `p install` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 7 1971) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ex yes`
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `p none` 5 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1985) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ex no b`
#ASSERT `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `p mining` 5 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1950) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ex none`

§§ `s 9(3): domestic services for others`

#ASSERT `Will I be compensated for my lost capacity to do domestic work for others` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dom yes`
#ASSERT `Will I be compensated for my lost capacity to do domestic work for others` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dom no loss`
#ASSERT `Will I be compensated for my lost capacity to do domestic work for others` `meso` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `dom none`

§§ `s 10: several defendants`

#ASSERT `Will my claim be decided before contribution between the defendants` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `order first`
#ASSERT `Will my claim be decided before contribution between the defendants` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `order together`
#ASSERT `Will my claim be decided before contribution between the defendants` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `order none`
#ASSERT `Will my claim be decided before contribution between the defendants` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `order none`

§§ `s 11: suing the insurer`

#ASSERT `Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `dead` TRUE EQUALS `ins yes`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `dissolved` TRUE EQUALS `ins yes`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `insolvent` TRUE EQUALS `ins yes`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `cannot be found` TRUE EQUALS `ins yes`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `none of these` TRUE EQUALS `ins no status`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly` `meso` TRUE TRUE TRUE `insolvent` FALSE EQUALS `ins no cover`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly` `other disease` FALSE TRUE TRUE `insolvent` TRUE EQUALS `ins none`

-- The cap: at, just under and just over the indemnity.
#ASSERT `How much can I recover from the insurer` 500000 400000 EQUALS 400000
#ASSERT `How much can I recover from the insurer` 400000 400000 EQUALS 400000
#ASSERT `How much can I recover from the insurer` 400001 400000 EQUALS 400000
#ASSERT `How much can I recover from the insurer` 399999 400000 EQUALS 399999
#ASSERT `How much can I recover from the insurer` 250000 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 11A: appeals from SAET`

#ASSERT `Where does my appeal go` TRUE `an interlocutory order` EQUALS `appeal single`
#ASSERT `Where does my appeal go` TRUE `any other decision` EQUALS `appeal ca`
#ASSERT `Where does my appeal go` FALSE `any other decision` EQUALS `appeal none`
